[5.817793, "o", "\u001b[H  \u001b[38;5;252mlocal history overlay rather than forwarded upstream. Point to the exact implementation symbols and\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mone existing focused test that directly asserts empty forwarded_input. Then suggest one small\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252madditional assertion.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;147m\r\n●\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1mTrace SSH wheel ownership\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n  railmux ssh — agent-pane wheel served locally, not forwarded upstream:\u001b[K\r\n  1. handle_terminal_part gets the SgrMouseEvent and dispatches to LocalHistoryView.wheel.\u001b[K\r\n  2. wheel() resolves the pane via _route_at; a hit on an agent viewport scrolls\u001b[K\r\n  _HistoryViewport.offset and returns HistoryAction with render_history=True and forwarded_input=b\"\" —\u001b[K\r\n  no upstream input.\u001b[K\r\n  3. apply_history_action only sends upstream when action.forwarded_input is set; empty means nothing\u001b[K\r\n  reaches tmux. The overlay is painted client-side via surface.paint_overlays.\u001b[K\r\n  4. This is a fast-client history overlay over bounded snapshots, not tmux copy-mode; the\u001b[K\r\n  implementation notes stock tmux WheelUpPane would enter copy-mode, which is deliberately avoided.\u001b[K\r\n  Focused test:\u001b[K\r\n  tests/test_fast_full_window.py::test_local_history_routes_sidebar_immediately_and_owns_agent_wheel\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;239m\r\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[38;5;147m\u001b[18;1H❯\u001b[39m Suggested addition: assert agent_action.render_history is True, proving the overlay rendered rather\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;239m\r\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[38;5;244m\u001b[20;1H  ⏵⏵ normal mode · shift+tab to cycle · ← for agents\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[48;5;70m\r\n[Railmux]\u001b[30m[Agent 1][Agent 2] Claude Code                                         \u001b[38;5;231m→ new session in railmux\u001b[30m \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[20;53H\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h"]
[5.817997, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h"]
